{"id": 7, "ts": 1780652771.6144738, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and rapid decision\u2011making, which are indeed vital. However, the same notes highlight that C \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d plus a low willingness to pursue further education. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, clear, collaborative communication and openness to learning are non\u2011negotiable; any barrier here can undermine crew coordination and safety.\nCandidate\u202fB, by contrast, is described as \u201cvery conscientious\u201d (a strong indicator of operational reliability) and \u201chandles stress very well\u201d (critical for the high\u2011pressure environment of international flights). His ability to assess weather conditions and his excellent computer skills also speak to solid technical competence. While B is noted as \u201cpretentious\u201d and sometimes adopts the wrong tone, these communication issues appear less severe than C\u2019s fundamental difficulty articulating ideas and egocentric attitude, and they can be mitigated through targeted coaching.\nGiven the balance of strengths and concerns, I would shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fB** as the better overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
